#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068858 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068458 :question/id #uuid "86e423e7-db4b-5fdf-a285-bded3bd8161e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12451" :question/problem "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050988 :topic/id #uuid "773e9f74-2606-5a7c-96ea-1dbef24812bb" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059714} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059715} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716}] :topic/math-academy-id 176 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050938} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051021}] :topic/title "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 2D"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051021 :topic/difficulty 0.7167474973411709 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428198 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompa